# API

* Reuse the existing API client/service architecture.
* Never invent endpoints.
* Never invent request parameters.
* Never invent response fields.
* Never assume backend behavior.
* Inspect existing API implementations before adding code.
* Reuse existing models and serialization patterns.
* Preserve existing authentication handling.
* Preserve existing error handling.
* Handle loading, success, empty, and error states where appropriate.
* Do not modify backend contracts from the Flutter app.

## Models

* Follow existing model naming and serialization.
* Reuse existing base classes/utilities.
* Do not duplicate models representing the same API resource.
* Do not add fields unless supported by the API.

## Errors

* Use existing error-handling utilities.
* Show localized user-friendly messages.
* Never expose stack traces or raw backend exceptions to users.
* Avoid logging sensitive response data.

## Requests

* Avoid duplicate API requests.
* Reuse existing caching where available.
* Do not introduce a new HTTP client.
* Do not add retry logic unless required.

## Security

* Never hardcode API secrets.
* Never commit credentials or private keys.
* Never log access tokens, passwords, payment data, or sensitive personal data.
